  "body": "## What changed\n\n- **`zenmux`** — new ZenMux gateway provider: `ReasoningObject`, `structured_reasoning_details`, `thinking_boolean_path` model list, `reasoning_delta_fallback_field`.\n- **`cline` upgraded in place** — kept the `cline` id + `CLINE_API_KEY` env (no rename, no user config breakage), but adopted upstream's richer profile: `DISABLED` reasoning replay, `structured_reasoning_details`, custom `/ai/cline/recommended-models` list.\n- **`OpenAIChatProfile`** gains `reasoning_delta_fallback_field` + `structured_reasoning_details` fields and a fallback-aware `reasoning_delta()`.\n- **Wired `_close_openai_tool_result_turns`** (deferred from v5.14.2): a `user` role following a `tool` role now inserts a synthetic assistant boundary — fixes a real upstream protocol bug where some OpenAI chat templates reject `user` directly after `tool` output.\n\n## Verification\n\n- Full suite: **3948 passed / 6 failed** (6 = pre-existing PowerShell-installer baseline).\n- `ruff format --check`, `ruff check`, `ty check`: all clean.\n- Two converter tests updated to the new role ordering + a new boundary test.\n\n## Residual risks\n\n- `cline`'s behavior change (THINK_TAGS → DISABLED replay + structured reasoning) is a provider-profile change for existing `cline` users — flagging it here; if a user's Cline deployment relied on the old reasoning replay, they should re-verify. This is why the id was kept: no config migration needed, just a behavior note.\n- `zenmux` has no live round-trip yet (no key available).\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)",
